{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
  "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen B. McCullough (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has again and again held that an arrest is constitutionally reasonable if the officers have probable cause to believe a suspect has committed a crime. The Court has found that this standard represents the best compromise between the needs of the citizens and the duty of the government to combat crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If this officer had complied with the State law, that is he had issued a summons, then you agree that the exclusionary rule would apply if he went ahead and searched."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State (Virginia)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0000-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the State argued below and the State court rejected was that he was alone in a car with this large angry dog."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The States and the Federal Government may for a variety of reasons enact restrictions on officer authority that exceed the requirements of the Fourth Amendment as this Court has articulated them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Virginia will not exclude evidence under its own State law for a violation of this provision. But it does say under State law that a person can resist an unlawful arrest, The officer can be sued for engaging in an unlawful arrest under State law, and that the officer can be fired or disciplined."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: If we rule for Respondent in this case, would we have to reexamine the holding in California v. Greenwood?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the same argument that Respondent is making here today: That California had renounced any interest in conducting garbage searches, therefore there's nothing on the State side of the line to balance against the individual's invasion of privacy, and therefore the State should lose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Thomas C. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF THOMAS C. GOLDSTEIN ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Right. But we're starting with a different premise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: If that -- if that logic is sound and that logic depends on Justice Powell's use of the word unlawfully, then it seems to me the -- the only way to arrest an irrational system would to be conclude that, in fact, the arrest is not constitutionally lawful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOLDSTEIN: Can I just correct one thing? And that is it does not depend on Justice Powell's use of the word unlawful. I believe to rule against us, Justice Souter, that you will have to overrule the line of cases from Di Re to DeFillipo."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What about Cooper -- Cooper v California?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Any crime at all; jaywalking, for example?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCullough",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We certainly think it strongly -- as the United States points out in their brief, that it strongly supports our position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCullough",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And as the lower courts have noted when facing a similar argument, you've already held that when it comes to a search, that under Greenwood and Cooper, that State-law considerations aren't going to be what the constitutional inquiry turns on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. McCullough, there is one thing that I was curious about. It is this Virginia law that allows the custodial arrest pursuant to an order of a general district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When is that used?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCullough",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a violation of state law, but it wasn't a constitutional problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would be the basis of a -- can a district court enter such an order just because it thinks it's a good idea? Are there any grounds in --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:05 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCullough",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b144d4e41926-0003-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute at issue, 46.2-936, does not really lay out particular criteria. So it is -- and the issue hasn't been litigated in the Virginia courts as to the criteria that's required. But it seems to be broad discretion by the general district judge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1082",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "b144d4e419265226fd3eefc82109704bc15e33b4ac4328cd1ae64ee2cf9d51fa",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-b144d4e41926-60",
